===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|fleute}}, {{m|enm|floute}}, {{m|enm|flote}}, from {{der|en|fro|flaute}}, from {{der|en|prv|flaut}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Perhaps ultimately from three possibilities:
* Blend of Provencal {{m|oc|flaujol|t=flageolet}} + {{m|oc|laut|t=[[lute]]}}
* From Latin {{m|la|flātus|t=blowing}}, from {{m|la|flāre|t=to blow}}
* Imitative.
{{doublet|en|flauta|fluyt}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[woodwind]] [[instrument]] consisting of a tube with a row of holes that produce sound through vibrations caused by air blown across the edge of the holes, often tuned by plugging one or more holes with a finger; the [[Western concert flute]], a [[transverse]] [[side-blown]] flute of European origin.
#* {{RQ:Pope Works|volume=I|title=January and May|page=217|passage=The breathing '''flute's''' ſoft notes are heard around, / And the ſhril trumpets mix their ſilver ſound; / The vaulted roofs vvith echoing muſic ring, / Theſe touch the vocal ſtops, and thoſe the trembling ſtring.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A [[recorder]], also a woodwind instrument.
# A [[glass]] with a long, narrow [[bowl]] and a long stem, used for drinking [[wine]], especially [[champagne]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=w:Sally Rooney|title=w:Normal People|chapter=Six Months Later (July  2013)|passage=These are champagne glasses, says Peggy.<br/>No, I mean the tall ones, Jamie says.<br/>You're thinking of '''flutes''', says Peggy. These are coupes.}}
# A lengthwise groove, such as one of the lengthwise grooves on a [[w:classical order|classical column]], or a groove on a cutting tool (such as a [[drill bit]], [[endmill]], or [[reamer]]), which helps to form both a cutting edge and a channel through which [[chip]]s can escape
# {{lb|en|architectural element|firearms}} A [[semicylindrical]] vertical groove, as in a [[pillar]], in [[plait]]ed [[cloth]], or in a rifle barrel to cut down the weight.
# A long [[French]] [[bread roll]], [[baguette]].<ref>{{R:Simmonds Trade}}</ref>
# An [[organ stop]] with a flute-like sound.
# A [[shuttle]] in [[weave|weaving]] [[tapestry]] etc.

